.TH V23-SELFTEST 1
.SH NAME
v23/selftest \- exercise Vanadium Limbo security primitives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B v23/selftest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I V23/selftest
runs in-process checks of
.IR v23-security (2):
principal creation, self-blessing, blessing another principal, encoding/
decoding, pattern matching, expiry caveats, and ACL checks.
It prints
.B ok
lines and exits 0 on success, or fails with a diagnostic.
.PP
It does not exercise
.IR v23-rpc (2)
over the network.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/v23/selftest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR v23-intro (2),
.IR v23-security (2),
.IR v23-principal (1)
.SH BUGS
.IP \(bu
Requires a working Keyring
.B %B
formatter in
.IR emu (1);
without
.B fmtinstall('B', big64conv)
in
.BR keyringmodinit ,
.B pktostr
/
.B certtostr
emit literal
.B %B%
and verify/encode tests fail.
.IP \(bu
Coverage is incomplete relative to Google Vanadium (no third-party caveats,
no VOM, no mount tables).
.SH TODO
.IP \(bu
Add encode→decode→verify round-trips that deliberately break digests.
.IP \(bu
Add a networked RPC selftest once dial timeouts exist.
